for I frame␀qp␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Constant quantization parameter rate control method␀qp_cb_offset␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Quantization parameter offset for cb channel␀qp_cr_offset␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Quantization parameter offset for cr channel␀no-scenecut␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀When lookahead is enabled, set this to 1 to disable adaptive I-frame insertion at scene cuts␀forced-idr␀If forcing keyframes, force them as IDR frames.␀b_adapt␀When lookahead is enabled, set this to 0 to disable adaptive B-frame decision␀spatial-aq␀set to 1 to enable Spatial AQ␀temporal-aq␀␀␀␀␀␀set to 1 to enable Temporal AQ␀zerolatency␀␀␀␀␀␀Set 1 to indicate zero latency operation (no reordering delay)␀nonref_p␀Set this to 1 to enable automatic insertion of non-reference P-frames␀strict_gop␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Set 1 to minimize GOP-to-GOP rate fluctuations␀aq-strength␀␀␀␀␀␀When Spatial AQ is enabled, this field is used to specify AQ strength. AQ strength scale is from 1 (low) - 15 (aggressive)␀weighted_pred␀Enable weighted prediction␀b_ref_mode␀Use B frames as references␀␀␀␀␀␀␀B frames will not be used for reference␀each␀␀␀␀Each B frame will be used for reference␀middle␀␀Only (number of B frames)/2 will be used for reference␀dpb_size␀Specifies the DPB size used for encoding (0 means automatic)␀ldkfs␀␀␀␀␀␀Low delay key frame scale; Specifies the Scene Change frame size increase allowed in case of single frame VBV and CBR␀intra-refresh␀␀␀␀␀Use Periodic Intra Refresh instead of IDR frames␀timing-info␀␀␀␀Include timing info in sequence/frame headers␀extra_sei␀Pass on extra SEI data (e.g. a53 cc) to be included in the bitstream␀a53cc␀␀␀␀␀␀Use A53 Closed Captions (if available)␀s12m_tc␀Use timecode (if available)␀lookahead_level␀␀␀␀␀␀Specifies the lookahead level. Higher level may improve quality at the expense of performance.␀split_encode_mode␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Specifies the split encoding mode␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Disabled for all configurations␀Enabled or disabled depending on the preset and tuning info␀forced␀␀␀␀␀␀Enabled with number of horizontal strips selected by the driver␀Enabled wi